<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teaching for Merikare</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Instruction for Merikare</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Teaching for Merikare is an ancient Egyptian wisdom text in which a king of the Herakleopolitan dynasty instructs his son Merikare on kingship, justice and the defence of the Delta frontier. Set in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-intermediate-period">First Intermediate Period</a>, it survives in copies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a> and may have been composed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-francia">Middle Kingdom</a>.</p></div>
